        "content": "<p>here is great</p>",
        "id": 611846400,
        "sender_full_name": "Luigi Massacci",
        "timestamp": 1784626231
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I am trying to do the following exercise: </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zero_mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">add_mul</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zero_add</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">nth_rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zero_add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">add_right_cancel</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The last line gives the following error: <code>Invalid rewrite argument: The pattern to be substituted is a metavariable (`?m.63`) in this equality</code>. I don't understand the error.</p>",
        "id": 611847448,
        "sender_full_name": "Eduardo de Lorenzo Poza",
        "timestamp": 1784626603
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have found that substituting the last line by </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">add_right_cancel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>finishes the proof, but I want to understand what I was doing wrong. What I wanted to do is take the current <code>h : 0 + 0 * a = 0 * a + 0 * a</code>, apply <code>add_right_cancel</code> to it, and then flip the equality to finish the proof. How can I do this?</p>",
        "id": 611851179,
        "sender_full_name": "Eduardo de Lorenzo Poza",
        "timestamp": 1784627900
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Can you please write a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mwe.html\">#mwe</a>?</p>",
        "id": 611851313,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1784627948
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think this should do</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Ring</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Defs</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Data</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Real</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyRing</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Ring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">add_right_cancel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">add_neg_cancel_right</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">add_neg_cancel_right</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zero_mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">add_mul</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zero_add</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">nth_rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zero_add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">add_right_cancel</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 611851416,
        "sender_full_name": "Eduardo de Lorenzo Poza",
        "timestamp": 1784627983
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Anyway if you want to apply theorem <code>foo</code> to the assumption <code>h</code> you can just write <code>apply foo at h</code>.</p>",
        "id": 611851593,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1784628030
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Indeed, you suggestion does exactly what I was looking for. But could you explain why the other approach with <code>rw</code> does not work?</p>",
        "id": 611856123,
        "sender_full_name": "Eduardo de Lorenzo Poza",
        "timestamp": 1784629620
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You can only rewrite an equality (or a double implication). Your theorem is an implication.</p>",
        "id": 611856256,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1784629665
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">add_right_cancel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>also works btw, which might be what you meant</p>",
        "id": 611856737,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1784629837
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I was expecting <code>add_right_cancel 0 (0 * a) (0 * a)</code> to be an instance of  <code>0 = 0 * a</code>, why doesn't this work?</p>",
        "id": 611856876,
        "sender_full_name": "Eduardo de Lorenzo Poza",
        "timestamp": 1784629887
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"933054\">Snir Broshi</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Eduardo.20de.20Lorenzo/near/611856737\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">add_right_cancel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>also works btw, which might be what you meant</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Indeed, this is more along the lines of what I was trying to do, but I was trying to rewrite at the hypothesis.</p>",
        "id": 611857166,
        "sender_full_name": "Eduardo de Lorenzo Poza",
        "timestamp": 1784630004
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1175902\">Eduardo de Lorenzo Poza</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Eduardo.20de.20Lorenzo/near/611856876\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I was expecting <code>add_right_cancel 0 (0 * a) (0 * a)</code> to be an instance of  <code>0 = 0 * a</code>, why doesn't this work?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>No, <code>add_right_cancel</code> wants an assumption <code>h</code> that says <code>a + b = c + b</code>, and then <code>add_right_cancel h</code> is the fact that <code>a = c</code>. So you have to give it the hypothesis to use it.</p>",
        "id": 611858269,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1784630405
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think it get it now, thanks!</p>",
        "id": 611858467,
        "sender_full_name": "Eduardo de Lorenzo Poza",
        "timestamp": 1784630489
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If your <code>a</code>, <code>b</code> and <code>c</code> are <code>0</code>, <code>0 * a</code> and <code>0 * a</code>, then <code>add_right_cancel</code> becomes: <em>if</em> <code>0 + 0 * a = 0 * a + 0 * a</code> then <code>0 = 0 * a</code>, but you still have to prove the if part.</p>",
        "id": 611858550,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1784630529
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But this is not why you get an error. Usually if you don't supply the hypothesis, lean leaves it as a new goal. But in this case, lean can't infer anything about the left hand side of the conclusion (<code>a</code>), so it complains that it can't figure out what you want to rewrite (\"is a metavariable\")</p>",
        "id": 611887227,
        "sender_full_name": "Ruben Van de Velde",
        "timestamp": 1784639746
    }
]